[{:db/id "q-331913/selection/66a229dc667b5617bcbb1d4e4298a5bec5f4b42f6b64a49e859257b3ce28f710" :answer/id #uuid "e01b0af9-30cd-50d7-a4ce-8a4cab6010b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331913/selection/01a694ae8c2e400a60563a72322b7de4a373d5dc6ee9b01a21efcd1c207da281" :answer/id #uuid "63e13ab9-4bd7-5fca-bdbe-a025c1b5a20a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331913/selection/d15a5d1d1ff36d403cfe682e83e05865057a3c32dddfcd849033ab8cdf05bdf0" :answer/id #uuid "814c8c66-e968-59ae-9762-36d350fd32ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331913/selection/6a071b534aebf45fcd195b8b75312a12e17d20e402230a6e8f738c70eba5bf59" :answer/id #uuid "51aa0b61-8028-55c6-8326-35c05b009b18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331913/selection/858e498f5f64f52c2d9d775e2598674dc81b1441482e80e0697eac59124bcdce" :answer/id #uuid "353adb76-84b2-5e81-b056-bcf86ce6ad7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331913/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5a2f420-7744-54b9-a957-1e22206a4137" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331913/selection/66a229dc667b5617bcbb1d4e4298a5bec5f4b42f6b64a49e859257b3ce28f710" :answer-field/choices ["q-331913/selection/66a229dc667b5617bcbb1d4e4298a5bec5f4b42f6b64a49e859257b3ce28f710" "q-331913/selection/01a694ae8c2e400a60563a72322b7de4a373d5dc6ee9b01a21efcd1c207da281" "q-331913/selection/d15a5d1d1ff36d403cfe682e83e05865057a3c32dddfcd849033ab8cdf05bdf0" "q-331913/selection/6a071b534aebf45fcd195b8b75312a12e17d20e402230a6e8f738c70eba5bf59" "q-331913/selection/858e498f5f64f52c2d9d775e2598674dc81b1441482e80e0697eac59124bcdce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331913" :question/id #uuid "9a519148-1dbb-52b2-8341-8fad4a34af30" :question/math-academy-id "q-331913" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=-{x}^{2}-2x+4.\n$$\n\nFind the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $ and $\\gamma ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n2(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+2(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-2x+4\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n2\\alpha {x}^{2}+(4\\alpha +2\\beta )x+(2\\beta +2\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-2x+4.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 4\\alpha +2\\beta =-2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 2\\beta +2\\gamma =4\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2},\\beta =0,\\gamma =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-331913/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf16afad-30ed-5055-a86c-28affd3d8930"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331913"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332550/selection/fcb62346f98a18a2322aa6b81e233d0ea3734467d0b55a34d1ddbf9dda5a7f61" :answer/id #uuid "06043398-b0d0-5555-9f49-23528d3e351c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+2x-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332550/selection/a5253ade8d39170937ce9df658ab3d6c872fa9ac4cc75de862194ea48328020f" :answer/id #uuid "3c3b017d-f699-5661-a43c-7724f21dea07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+4x-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332550/selection/01920d15d82c5b1ff4fcf697f8a04b3dc69d9c08581077e14202f7a61fe5b645" :answer/id #uuid "c49dfca2-94c5-548e-9baf-9a2ef97c8f5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-3{x}^{2}+4x-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332550/selection/4134ece82751b3b6a11925d1eca9bdab1f20c167e1aa58f953a48bc5b5345ab9" :answer/id #uuid "29ea374a-ef1b-5dd5-b782-6931263baaee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+4x+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332550/selection/6831a43260bdcc843a214e09a034dc1f5a1ddbe14916d7cc2181d407c380de42" :answer/id #uuid "b5cea147-d03b-5fc5-9000-9eae8db49959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}-4x-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332550/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d95ee038-e4e0-565c-9eea-daade6a92927" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332550/selection/a5253ade8d39170937ce9df658ab3d6c872fa9ac4cc75de862194ea48328020f" :answer-field/choices ["q-332550/selection/fcb62346f98a18a2322aa6b81e233d0ea3734467d0b55a34d1ddbf9dda5a7f61" "q-332550/selection/a5253ade8d39170937ce9df658ab3d6c872fa9ac4cc75de862194ea48328020f" "q-332550/selection/01920d15d82c5b1ff4fcf697f8a04b3dc69d9c08581077e14202f7a61fe5b645" "q-332550/selection/4134ece82751b3b6a11925d1eca9bdab1f20c167e1aa58f953a48bc5b5345ab9" "q-332550/selection/6831a43260bdcc843a214e09a034dc1f5a1ddbe14916d7cc2181d407c380de42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332550" :question/id #uuid "09b19c17-c03f-56ab-a743-01f7ab8d8701" :question/math-academy-id "q-332550" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-{x}^{2}+2x-3.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $, and $\\gamma $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$  we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+2x-3\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\alpha {x}^{2}+(2\\alpha +\\beta )x+(\\beta +\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+2x-3\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 2\\alpha +\\beta =2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\beta +\\gamma =-3\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,\\beta =4,\\gamma =-7.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-{x}^{2}+4x-7.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+4x-7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-332550/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f120ae90-3df2-56d4-8a21-38c801f60d72"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332550"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332552/selection/dc569edadd48e41539c28822e7215348752ed4451468f353a4150a11f0ff575f" :answer/id #uuid "7bf58d12-f56b-5546-befb-36d9d93221da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}-x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332552/selection/bd65366ff2e251ba02aa88c91212d703a3bc004d99dcd7e08a71f0ae53ddb1a7" :answer/id #uuid "7a20d413-26f0-53ee-bc1a-c4257a359af2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}-x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332552/selection/cb2ade70e6e6a6650b547c3a7ca7b80bdf3105b30a71fa205aadbf27aa6004ae" :answer/id #uuid "2d19cfcc-2113-534f-87de-bc729ec24926" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332552/selection/5ddccd7130a8398bffee3a8beca746acf7e4b0455107604fd5123db8f287a0a0" :answer/id #uuid "bf225a9f-68f4-5c7b-87f3-dfde75d31e24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332552/selection/6d5e3a7d1511d07f5282b3de2268572c62658129b436e9eb4c6da28f3218d8b2" :answer/id #uuid "dd622a14-745d-5bc4-82e9-e678a61adfea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332552/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "42c0e438-2e2c-5a8e-abc3-67f8997c9f4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-332552/selection/cb2ade70e6e6a6650b547c3a7ca7b80bdf3105b30a71fa205aadbf27aa6004ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-332552/selection/dc569edadd48e41539c28822e7215348752ed4451468f353a4150a11f0ff575f" "q-332552/selection/bd65366ff2e251ba02aa88c91212d703a3bc004d99dcd7e08a71f0ae53ddb1a7" "q-332552/selection/cb2ade70e6e6a6650b547c3a7ca7b80bdf3105b30a71fa205aadbf27aa6004ae" "q-332552/selection/5ddccd7130a8398bffee3a8beca746acf7e4b0455107604fd5123db8f287a0a0" "q-332552/selection/6d5e3a7d1511d07f5282b3de2268572c62658129b436e9eb4c6da28f3218d8b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332552" :question/id #uuid "21fc98d5-a07a-53e9-b823-65887e0c4938" :question/math-academy-id "q-332552" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-{x}^{2}-x-1.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $, and $\\gamma $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$  we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-x-1\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\alpha {x}^{2}+(2\\alpha +\\beta )x+(\\beta +\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-x-1\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 2\\alpha +\\beta =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\beta +\\gamma =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,\\beta =1,\\gamma =-2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-{x}^{2}+x-2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+x-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-332552/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f120ae90-3df2-56d4-8a21-38c801f60d72"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332552"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332756/field-1/c49884cac74f688f11aefc5bd0f78693d3083279ebab41f8c5c272dbbbc63606" :answer/id #uuid "7fce7db3-d92c-5ce9-98d7-1a029894054e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}e^{-3x}-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332756/field-1/dcec8bd9e578fb395cc064db207052229cd63841e93a16ddde623353071ba212" :answer/id #uuid "ece7ff4a-4703-5d30-a758-2d0eaa64f87a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}e^{-3x}-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332756/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dda6553-3ca9-5906-bdf1-513ea7bac620" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332756/field-1/c49884cac74f688f11aefc5bd0f78693d3083279ebab41f8c5c272dbbbc63606" :answer-field/choices ["q-332756/field-1/c49884cac74f688f11aefc5bd0f78693d3083279ebab41f8c5c272dbbbc63606" "q-332756/field-1/dcec8bd9e578fb395cc064db207052229cd63841e93a16ddde623353071ba212"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332756" :question/id #uuid "d2079c55-b54d-5179-8b5d-5fa6fd0d212f" :question/math-academy-id "q-332756" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+3y=-6x+1,\\,y(0)=\\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+3y=-6x+1\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{-3x},$ solve the initial value problem.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\alpha +3(\\alpha x+\\beta )=-6x+1\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\alpha x+(\\alpha +3\\beta )=-6x+1\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\alpha =-6\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\alpha +3\\beta =1\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-2,\\,\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2x+1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}-2x+1.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=\\frac{5}{3}$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-3(0)}-2(0)+1 & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ A+1 & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ A & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-3x}-2x+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332756/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34158a33-c6b6-55dc-a4a7-2b5c1c753ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332756"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332782/field-1/0e1daca87f884d59409afa338e65f379e5862eef78684aab567962d3d7f4c3e4" :answer/id #uuid "9b887604-2cc7-5490-a98e-ba00780d40f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-e^{-5x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332782/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f821175-a091-589f-be58-2ee16889c49a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332782/field-1/0e1daca87f884d59409afa338e65f379e5862eef78684aab567962d3d7f4c3e4" :answer-field/choices ["q-332782/field-1/0e1daca87f884d59409afa338e65f379e5862eef78684aab567962d3d7f4c3e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332782" :question/id #uuid "6ab36fa8-faf8-5e3a-8a1b-c1cff952273e" :question/math-academy-id "q-332782" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+5y=10,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+5y=10\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{-5x},$ solve the initial value problem.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-5x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a constant, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\beta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\beta $ is a constant to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0+5\\beta =10\n$$\n\nSolving for $\\beta $ gives $\\beta =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+2.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{0}+2 & =1 \\\\ A+2 & =1 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-5x}+2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-332782/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "34158a33-c6b6-55dc-a4a7-2b5c1c753ac6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332782"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
